  "stakes": {
    "do": "Buy a rail-spur lot from Ezra Lowry, sell wagon and craft work, get a dispute ruled on by Magistrate Holt.",
    "lose": "A lot's whole purchase price if the spur never comes, which is the bet Lowry is selling and Reverend Pike has buried men over.",
    "decide": "Whether the county hears Prisca Montaigne's true account of what happened out on the grass, or Silas Cobbett's better one."
  },
  "art_gap": "Reads as an open lot with camp props and new fence. Needs half-raised frame buildings, canvas tents beside finished walls, and a steepleless church. The 'boomtown' is entirely in the ground tint and the crowd right now."
